{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ada’s first visionOS milestone is windowed rendering. Apps launch as normal visionOS windows backed by UIKit scenes, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MTKView"},{"type":"text","text":", and the Metal render backend. Existing apps that use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" do not need a new public API for this mode."}]},{"code":["import AdaEngine","","@main","struct VisionOSWindowedApp: App {","    var body: some AppScene {","        WindowGroup {","            Text(\"Ada on visionOS\")","                .padding()","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Windowed mode intentionally does not create a Full Space, stereo renderer, ARKit session, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompositorServices.LayerRenderer"},{"type":"text","text":" surface. Those belong to a later immersive rendering milestone."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/VisionOSWindowed","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run Ada apps in visionOS Shared Space using the existing "},{"code":"WindowGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" scene model."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/DLSSUpscaling","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ProceduralNoise"]}],"metadata":{"title":"visionOS Windowed Mode","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"AdaEngine"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adaengine\/visionoswindowed"]}],"references":{"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationIK":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Constrain a skeletal chain after its clip, Animation Graph and visual LOD pose have been mixed."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationik","type":"topic","title":"Animation IK and pose modifiers","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/ProceduralNoise":{"abstract":[{"text":"Use a noise generator as a deterministic scalar field for terrain heights,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"procedural placement, or volume density. Import "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, or use its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-export from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdaEngine"},{"type":"text","text":". No GPU or editor state is needed."}],"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/proceduralnoise","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Procedural Noise","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ProceduralNoise"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AdaUIIdentity":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/adauiidentity","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"AdaUI reconciles a new view tree against the mounted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ViewNode"},{"text":" tree. A node is preserved only when the new node and old node describe the same identity and the new node can update the old node. Preserved nodes keep their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", focus state, in-flight animation controllers, layers, and other node-local runtime state. Recreated nodes start with fresh runtime state."}],"type":"topic","title":"AdaUI View Identity"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/MovieMaker":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a fresh game world at a fixed simulation rate, waiting for every GPU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame and disk write before advancing. Rendering speed never drops movie frames."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Configure the same gameplay plugins and cameras as your game in "},{"code":"make","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Platform\/window plugins are unnecessary for this offscreen runtime."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MovieMaker","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/moviemaker","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}]},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Atmosphere":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/atmosphere","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give a 3D camera a physically based sky. The atmosphere scatters the sun’s light"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the way air does, so the sky turns from blue at noon to orange near the horizon","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and dark at night, the sun appears as a disc that the air reddens, and distant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry fades into haze."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Atmosphere","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine":{"abstract":[{"text":"Bringing simple and powerful game engine for your awesome games.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine","kind":"symbol","title":"AdaEngine"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Contributing":{"abstract":[{"text":"We welcome contributions of all kinds: bug fixes, features, documentation, and examples.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Contributing to Ada","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/contributing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/GameDiagnosticsOverlay":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See the game’s update rate while you play. The overlay shows "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FPS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Frame time"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the top-left corner of the game window. Mouse and keyboard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"input still reach the game under the overlay.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Game diagnostics overlay","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/gamediagnosticsoverlay"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/HardwarePathTracing":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let a path-traced view find ray intersections with the GPU’s ray-tracing hardware instead of a shader BVH. The image,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lighting and denoisers stay the same; only the intersection step changes, and the shader BVH remains the fallback"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wherever hardware cannot be used.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/hardwarepathtracing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Hardware Path Tracing","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/ImageDecoders":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/imagedecoders","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Load PNG, JPEG (","type":"text"},{"code":"jpg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"jpeg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), BMP and TGA images as CPU pixels using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or load a GPU texture through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Texture2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Loading images and adding formats"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/CharacterLocomotion3D":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/characterlocomotion3d","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CharacterLocomotion3DComponent"},{"type":"text","text":" to play skeletal animations from an upright 3D character’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"actual movement. Add it to the root entity that owns the character controller and skinned model."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Your input or AI continues to set "},{"code":"desiredVelocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jumpRequested"},{"type":"text","text":". Locomotion reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"resolved motion after physics, so holding forward against a wall can leave the character idle.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Animate a 3D character from movement"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationAuthoring":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationauthoring","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Copy an imported animation or capture a rest\/current pose into a project-owned"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animlib"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. Source GLB\/glTF bytes remain unchanged. Swift code, Studio’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Animator, the editor agent and project Tools share the same data and edit commands.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Authoring skeletal animation","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/DLSSUpscaling":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/DLSSUpscaling","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/dlssupscaling","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Render a 3D view below its output resolution and reconstruct it with NVIDIA DLSS Super Resolution, or denoise a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path-traced view with DLSS Ray Reconstruction. DLSS is optional: without it a camera uses the portable temporal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction that ships with the engine, and nothing else changes."}],"type":"topic","title":"DLSS Upscaling"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Terrain":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/terrain","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create editable ground with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Terrain3D"},{"type":"text","text":". Its heights describe one square surface"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the entity’s local X\/Z plane. "},{"code":"Model3DPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates the visible geometry;","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Physics3DPlugin"},{"text":" adds matching static triangle collision.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Terrain","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Building":{"abstract":[{"text":"This guide covers two scenarios:","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Building Ada","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/building"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/PipelinedRendering":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/pipelinedrendering","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Render a scene one frame behind its simulation to overlap rendering with the next frame’s work."}],"type":"topic","title":"Pipelined Rendering"}}}